-- title:
--   Unramified decomposition group is cyclic
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ and $K$ be number fields with $K$ an $E$-algebra such that $K/E$ is Galois, and let $w$ be a point of the height-one spectrum of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_K$, i.e. a nonzero prime ideal of $\mathcal{O}_K$. Write $v = w \cap \mathcal{O}_E$ for the prime of $\mathcal{O}_E$ lying under $w$, and assume that the ramification index of the prime ideal of $v$ in the prime ideal of $w$ equals $1$, i.e. $e(w\mid v) = 1$. The conclusion is that the group [`NumberField.PlaceDecomp.decomp E K w`](def/NumberField_PlaceDecompositionAction.html#L82) is cyclic, where by definition this is the decomposition subgroup, inside the group $K \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[E]} K$ of $E$-algebra automorphisms of $K$, of the valuation subring attached to the $w$-adic valuation of $K$: the subgroup of those automorphisms over $E$ that preserve that valuation subring. Thus: at an unramified prime of a Galois extension of number fields, the decomposition group is cyclic.
--
--   This is the standard fact that a decomposition group at an unramified prime is cyclic, being generated by a Frobenius element. It is used to supply the cyclicity needed for the local Tate cohomology computations of unit groups at unramified places, via [`NumberField.PlaceDecomp.subsingleton_tateCohomology_integerUnits_of_ramificationIdx_eq_one`](thm.html#NumberField.PlaceDecomp.subsingleton_tateCohomology_integerUnits_of_ramificationIdx_eq_one).
